GIZ - Portfolio Manager

The German Development Cooperation through GIZ is looking for a national Portfolio Manager within its Country Office in the Republic of Moldova.

This part-time position is expected to start on the 15th of June 2024 for a 6-month period.The permanent workplace of the Portfolio Manager will be located within the facilities of the GIZ Country Office in Chisinau.

The overall responsibilities related to this position are as follows: 

  • providing professional advisory services to the Country Director (CD) and the Project Managers (PM) on portfolio and commissioning, on use of relevant instruments, on integration of cross-cutting issues (gender, diversity, digitalization, quality, monitoring) and on acquisition of new commissions;
  • supporting the CD in preparing, steering and further developing the portfolio;
  • providing specialist advice to project managers in identifying opportunities for inclusion of new stakeholders;
  • assisting the CD in planning and monitoring the annual objectives, assuring the quality of the offer and reporting system related to commissions;
  • advising and coordinating meetings in the field of foreign affairs, audits and project evaluation visits, consistently ensuring the implementation of the business policy for the region and general objectives;
  • ensuring a smooth realization for the start-up of new projects, including registration of projects with the State Chancellery.

Required qualifications:

  • Bachelor and/or Master Degree in one of the following subjects: Economics, Journalism, Business Administration, IT or in other related areas;
  • at least 5 years of professional working experience, ideally in business development and international cooperation, with a focus on the Public Relations, communication and IT;
  • experience within and deep understanding of the International Economic Development and Cooperation;
  • be able to work autonomously and on own initiative while reporting regularly to the CD;
