The permanent workplace of the Portfolio Manager will be located within the facilities of the GIZ Country Office in Chisinau.

The overall responsibilities related to this position are as follows: 

    • providing professional advisory services to the Country Director (CD) and the Project Managers (PM) on portfolio and commissioning, on use of relevant instruments, on integration of cross-cutting issues (gender, diversity, digitalization, quality, monitoring) and on acquisition of new commissions;
    • supporting the CD in preparing intergovernmental consultations and negotiations, steering and further developing the portfolio, identifying new economic sectors with high potential for acquisition of new projects;
    • providing specialist advice to project managers in identifying opportunities for inclusion of new stakeholders;
    • assisting the CD in planning and monitoring the annual objectives, assuring the quality of the offer and reporting system related to commissions;
    • advising and coordinating meetings in the field of foreign affairs, audits and project evaluation visits, consistently ensuring the implementation of the business policy for the region and general objectives;
    • preparation and management of small individual measures with budget responsibility;  
    • coordinating and advising GIZ projects on the external public communications issues, relations with the media, information and awareness; providing consultancy and support in communication for press and communication officers of GIZ stakeholders;
  • facilitating the increase of public information and awareness regarding achievements of GIZ projects in cooperation with the project communication officers, providing support in implementation of the communication strategy; 
  • establishing and maintaining media partnerships for coverage of the GIZ-project activities, monitoring media on the clippings on GIZ projects activities;

